<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">British Commonwealth Air Training Plan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1939">1939</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The British Commonwealth Air Training Plan was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> programme for training aircrew from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> and other Allied countries, run largely in Canada, far from enemy action. Agreed in December 1939, it trained more than 130,000 pilots, navigators, gunners and other aircrew at over a hundred schools, and was one of Canada's main contributions to the Allied air war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/british-commonwealth-air-training-plan.jpg" alt="British Commonwealth Air Training Plan" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: J.Klank · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harvard_t6_d-frcp.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
